#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:140
msgid "Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:142
msgid "Cookie object properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:144
msgid "_key_ - string - the name or key of the cookie (default \"\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:145
msgid "_value_ - string - the value of the cookie (default \"\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:146
msgid ""
"_expires_ - `Date` - if set, the `Expires=` attribute of the cookie "
"(defaults to the string `\"Infinity\"`). See `setExpires()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:147
msgid ""
"_maxAge_ - seconds - if set, the `Max-Age=` attribute _in seconds_ of the"
" cookie.  May also be set to strings `\"Infinity\"` and `\"-Infinity\"` "
"for non-expiry and immediate-expiry, respectively.  See `setMaxAge()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:148
msgid "_domain_ - string - the `Domain=` attribute of the cookie"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:149
msgid "_path_ - string - the `Path=` of the cookie"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:150
msgid "_secure_ - boolean - the `Secure` cookie flag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:151
msgid "_httpOnly_ - boolean - the `HttpOnly` cookie flag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:152
msgid ""
"_extensions_ - `Array` - any unrecognized cookie attributes as strings "
"(even if equal-signs inside)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:153
msgid "_creation_ - `Date` - when this cookie was constructed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:154
msgid ""
"_creationIndex_ - number - set at construction, used to provide greater "
"sort precision (please see `cookieCompare(a,b)` for a full explanation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:156
msgid ""
"After a cookie has been passed through `CookieJar.setCookie()` it will "
"have the following additional attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:158
msgid ""
"_hostOnly_ - boolean - is this a host-only cookie (i.e. no Domain field "
"was set, but was instead implied)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:159
msgid ""
"_pathIsDefault_ - boolean - if true, there was no Path field on the "
"cookie and `defaultPath()` was used to derive one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:160
msgid ""
"_creation_ - `Date` - **modified** from construction to when the cookie "
"was added to the jar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:161
msgid ""
"_lastAccessed_ - `Date` - last time the cookie got accessed. Will affect "
"cookie cleaning once implemented.  Using `cookiejar.getCookies(...)` will"
" update this attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:163
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`Cookie([{properties}])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:165
msgid ""
"Receives an options object that can contain any of the above Cookie "
"properties, uses the default for unspecified properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:167
msgid "`.toString()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:169
msgid ""
"encode to a Set-Cookie header value.  The Expires cookie field is set "
"using `formatDate()`, but is omitted entirely if `.expires` is "
"`Infinity`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:171
msgid "`.cookieString()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:173
msgid ""
"encode to a Cookie header value (i.e. the `.key` and `.value` properties "
"joined with '=')."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:175
msgid "`.setExpires(String)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:177
msgid ""
"sets the expiry based on a date-string passed through `parseDate()`.  If "
"parseDate returns `null` (i.e. can't parse this date string), `.expires` "
"is set to `\"Infinity\"` (a string) is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:179
msgid "`.setMaxAge(number)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:181
msgid ""
"sets the maxAge in seconds.  Coerces `-Infinity` to `\"-Infinity\"` and "
"`Infinity` to `\"Infinity\"` so it JSON serializes correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:183
msgid "`.expiryTime([now=Date.now()])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:185
msgid "`.expiryDate([now=Date.now()])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:187
msgid ""
"expiryTime() Computes the absolute unix-epoch milliseconds that this "
"cookie expires. expiryDate() works similarly, except it returns a `Date` "
"object.  Note that in both cases the `now` parameter should be "
"milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:189
msgid ""
"Max-Age takes precedence over Expires (as per the RFC). The `.creation` "
"attribute -- or, by default, the `now` parameter -- is used to offset the"
" `.maxAge` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:191
msgid "If Expires (`.expires`) is set, that's returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:193
msgid ""
"Otherwise, `expiryTime()` returns `Infinity` and `expiryDate()` returns a"
" `Date` object for \"Tue, 19 Jan 2038 03:14:07 GMT\" (latest date that "
"can be expressed by a 32-bit `time_t`; the common limit for most user-"
"agents)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:195
msgid "`.TTL([now=Date.now()])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:197
msgid ""
"compute the TTL relative to `now` (milliseconds).  The same precedence "
"rules as for `expiryTime`/`expiryDate` apply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:199
msgid ""
"The \"number\" `Infinity` is returned for cookies without an explicit "
"expiry and `0` is returned if the cookie is expired.  Otherwise a time-"
"to-live in milliseconds is returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:201
msgid "`.canonicalizedDomain()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:203
msgid "`.cdomain()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:205
msgid ""
"return the canonicalized `.domain` field.  This is lower-cased and "
"punycode (RFC3490) encoded if the domain has any non-ASCII characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:207
#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:323
msgid "`.toJSON()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:209
msgid ""
"For convenience in using `JSON.serialize(cookie)`. Returns a plain-old "
"`Object` that can be JSON-serialized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:211
msgid ""
"Any `Date` properties (i.e., `.expires`, `.creation`, and "
"`.lastAccessed`) are exported in ISO format (`.toISOString()`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:213
msgid ""
"**NOTE**: Custom `Cookie` properties will be discarded. In tough-cookie "
"1.x, since there was no `.toJSON` method explicitly defined, all "
"enumerable properties were captured. If you want a property to be "
"serialized, add the property name to the `Cookie.serializableProperties` "
"Array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:215
msgid "`Cookie.fromJSON(strOrObj)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:217
msgid ""
"Does the reverse of `cookie.toJSON()`. If passed a string, will "
"`JSON.parse()` that first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:219
msgid ""
"Any `Date` properties (i.e., `.expires`, `.creation`, and "
"`.lastAccessed`) are parsed via `Date.parse()`, not the tough-cookie "
"`parseDate`, since it's JavaScript/JSON-y timestamps being handled at "
"this layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:221
msgid "Returns `null` upon JSON parsing error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:223
msgid "`.clone()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:225
msgid ""
"Does a deep clone of this cookie, exactly implemented as "
"`Cookie.fromJSON(cookie.toJSON())`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:227
msgid "`.validate()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:229
msgid ""
"Status: *IN PROGRESS*. Works for a few things, but is by no means "
"comprehensive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:231
msgid ""
"validates cookie attributes for semantic correctness.  Useful for "
"\"lint\" checking any Set-Cookie headers you generate.  For now, it "
"returns a boolean, but eventually could return a reason string -- you can"
" future-proof with this construct:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:242
msgid "CookieJar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:244
msgid "Exported via `tough.CookieJar`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:246
msgid "`CookieJar([store],[options])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:248
msgid ""
"Simply use `new CookieJar()`.  If you'd like to use a custom store, pass "
"that to the constructor otherwise a `MemoryCookieStore` will be created "
"and used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:250
#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:262
#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:281
msgid "The `options` object can be omitted and can have the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:252
msgid ""
"_rejectPublicSuffixes_ - boolean - default `true` - reject cookies with "
"domains like \"com\" and \"co.uk\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:253
msgid ""
"_looseMode_ - boolean - default `false` - accept malformed cookies like "
"`bar` and `=bar`, which have an implied empty name. This is not in the "
"standard, but is used sometimes on the web and is accepted by (most) "
"browsers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:256
msgid ""
"Since eventually this module would like to support database/remote/etc. "
"CookieJars, continuation passing style is used for CookieJar methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:258
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`.setCookie(cookieOrString, currentUrl, [{options},] cb(err,cookie))`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:260
msgid ""
"Attempt to set the cookie in the cookie jar.  If the operation fails, an "
"error will be given to the callback `cb`, otherwise the cookie is passed "
"through.  The cookie will have updated `.creation`, `.lastAccessed` and "
"`.hostOnly` properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:264
#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:283
msgid ""
"_http_ - boolean - default `true` - indicates if this is an HTTP or non-"
"HTTP API.  Affects HttpOnly cookies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:265
#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:284
msgid ""
"_secure_ - boolean - autodetect from url - indicates if this is a "
"\"Secure\" API.  If the currentUrl starts with `https:` or `wss:` then "
"this is defaulted to `true`, otherwise `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:266
#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:285
msgid ""
"_now_ - Date - default `new Date()` - what to use for the creation/access"
" time of cookies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:267
msgid ""
"_ignoreError_ - boolean - default `false` - silently ignore things like "
"parse errors and invalid domains.  `Store` errors aren't ignored by this "
"option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:269
msgid ""
"As per the RFC, the `.hostOnly` property is set if there was no "
"\"Domain=\" parameter in the cookie string (or `.domain` was null on the "
"Cookie object).  The `.domain` property is set to the fully-qualified "
"hostname of `currentUrl` in this case.  Matching this cookie requires an "
"exact hostname match (not a `domainMatch` as per usual)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:271
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`.setCookieSync(cookieOrString, currentUrl, [{options}])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:273
msgid ""
"Synchronous version of `setCookie`; only works with synchronous stores "
"(e.g. the default `MemoryCookieStore`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:275
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`.getCookies(currentUrl, [{options},] cb(err,cookies))`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:277
msgid ""
"Retrieve the list of cookies that can be sent in a Cookie header for the "
"current url."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:279
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"If an error is encountered, that's passed as `err` to the callback, "
"otherwise an `Array` of `Cookie` objects is passed.  The array is sorted "
"with `cookieCompare()` unless the `{sort:false}` option is given."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:286
msgid ""
"_expire_ - boolean - default `true` - perform expiry-time checking of "
"cookies and asynchronously remove expired cookies from the store.  Using "
"`false` will return expired cookies and **not** remove them from the "
"store (which is useful for replaying Set-Cookie headers, potentially)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:287
msgid ""
"_allPaths_ - boolean - default `false` - if `true`, do not scope cookies "
"by path. The default uses RFC-compliant path scoping. **Note**: may not "
"be supported by the underlying store (the default `MemoryCookieStore` "
"supports it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:289
msgid ""
"The `.lastAccessed` property of the returned cookies will have been "
"updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:291
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`.getCookiesSync(currentUrl, [{options}])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:293
msgid ""
"Synchronous version of `getCookies`; only works with synchronous stores "
"(e.g. the default `MemoryCookieStore`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:295
msgid "`.getCookieString(...)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:297
msgid ""
"Accepts the same options as `.getCookies()` but passes a string suitable "
"for a Cookie header rather than an array to the callback.  Simply maps "
"the `Cookie` array via `.cookieString()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:299
msgid "`.getCookieStringSync(...)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:301
msgid ""
"Synchronous version of `getCookieString`; only works with synchronous "
"stores (e.g. the default `MemoryCookieStore`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:303
msgid "`.getSetCookieStrings(...)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:305
msgid ""
"Returns an array of strings suitable for **Set-Cookie** headers. Accepts "
"the same options as `.getCookies()`.  Simply maps the cookie array via "
"`.toString()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:307
msgid "`.getSetCookieStringsSync(...)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:309
msgid ""
"Synchronous version of `getSetCookieStrings`; only works with synchronous"
" stores (e.g. the default `MemoryCookieStore`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:311
msgid "`.serialize(cb(err,serializedObject))`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:313
msgid "Serialize the Jar if the underlying store supports `.getAllCookies`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:315
msgid ""
"**NOTE**: Custom `Cookie` properties will be discarded. If you want a "
"property to be serialized, add the property name to the "
"`Cookie.serializableProperties` Array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:317
msgid "See [Serialization Format]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:319
msgid "`.serializeSync()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:321
msgid "Sync version of .serialize"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:325
msgid ""
"Alias of .serializeSync() for the convenience of "
"`JSON.stringify(cookiejar)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:327
msgid "`CookieJar.deserialize(serialized, [store], cb(err,object))`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:329
msgid ""
"A new Jar is created and the serialized Cookies are added to the "
"underlying store. Each `Cookie` is added via `store.putCookie` in the "
"order in which they appear in the serialization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:331
msgid ""
"The `store` argument is optional, but should be an instance of `Store`. "
"By default, a new instance of `MemoryCookieStore` is created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:333
msgid ""
"As a convenience, if `serialized` is a string, it is passed through "
"`JSON.parse` first. If that throws an error, this is passed to the "
"callback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:335
msgid "`CookieJar.deserializeSync(serialized, [store])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:337
msgid ""
"Sync version of `.deserialize`.  _Note_ that the `store` must be "
"synchronous for this to work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:339
msgid "`CookieJar.fromJSON(string)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:341
msgid ""
"Alias of `.deserializeSync` to provide consistency with "
"`Cookie.fromJSON()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:343
msgid "`.clone([store,]cb(err,newJar))`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:345
msgid ""
"Produces a deep clone of this jar. Modifications to the original won't "
"affect the clone, and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:347
msgid ""
"The `store` argument is optional, but should be an instance of `Store`. "
"By default, a new instance of `MemoryCookieStore` is created. "
"Transferring between store types is supported so long as the source "
"implements `.getAllCookies()` and the destination implements "
"`.putCookie()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:349
msgid "`.cloneSync([store])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:351
msgid "Synchronous version of `.clone`, returning a new `CookieJar` instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:353
msgid ""
"The `store` argument is optional, but must be a _synchronous_ `Store` "
"instance if specified. If not passed, a new instance of "
"`MemoryCookieStore` is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:355
msgid ""
"The _source_ and _destination_ must both be synchronous `Store`s. If one "
"or both stores are asynchronous, use `.clone` instead. Recall that "
"`MemoryCookieStore` supports both synchronous and asynchronous API calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:357
msgid "`.removeAllCookies(cb(err))`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:359
msgid "Removes all cookies from the jar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:361
msgid ""
"This is a new backwards-compatible feature of `tough-cookie` version 2.5,"
" so not all Stores will implement it efficiently. For Stores that do not "
"implement `removeAllCookies`, the fallback is to call `removeCookie` "
"after `getAllCookies`. If `getAllCookies` fails or isn't implemented in "
"the Store, that error is returned. If one or more of the `removeCookie` "
"calls fail, only the first error is returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:363
msgid "`.removeAllCookiesSync()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:365
msgid "Sync version of `.removeAllCookies()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:367
msgid "Store"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:369
msgid "Base class for CookieJar stores. Available as `tough.Store`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:371
msgid "Store API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:373
msgid ""
"The storage model for each `CookieJar` instance can be replaced with a "
"custom implementation.  The default is `MemoryCookieStore` which can be "
"found in the `lib/memstore.js` file.  The API uses continuation-passing-"
"style to allow for asynchronous stores."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:375
msgid ""
"Stores should inherit from the base `Store` class, which is available as "
"`require('tough-cookie').Store`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:377
msgid ""
"Stores are asynchronous by default, but if `store.synchronous` is set to "
"`true`, then the `*Sync` methods on the of the containing `CookieJar` can"
" be used (however, the continuation-passing style"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:379
msgid "All `domain` parameters will have been normalized before calling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:381
msgid "The Cookie store must have all of the following methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:383
msgid "`store.findCookie(domain, path, key, cb(err,cookie))`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:385
msgid ""
"Retrieve a cookie with the given domain, path and key (a.k.a. name).  The"
" RFC maintains that exactly one of these cookies should exist in a store."
"  If the store is using versioning, this means that the latest/newest "
"such cookie should be returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:387
msgid ""
"Callback takes an error and the resulting `Cookie` object.  If no cookie "
"is found then `null` MUST be passed instead (i.e. not an error)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:389
msgid "`store.findCookies(domain, path, cb(err,cookies))`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:391
msgid ""
"Locates cookies matching the given domain and path.  This is most often "
"called in the context of `cookiejar.getCookies()` above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:393
msgid "If no cookies are found, the callback MUST be passed an empty array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:395
msgid ""
"The resulting list will be checked for applicability to the current "
"request according to the RFC (domain-match, path-match, http-only-flag, "
"secure-flag, expiry, etc.), so it's OK to use an optimistic search "
"algorithm when implementing this method.  However, the search algorithm "
"used SHOULD try to find cookies that `domainMatch()` the domain and "
"`pathMatch()` the path in order to limit the amount of checking that "
"needs to be done."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:397
msgid ""
"As of version 0.9.12, the `allPaths` option to `cookiejar.getCookies()` "
"above will cause the path here to be `null`.  If the path is `null`, "
"path-matching MUST NOT be performed (i.e. domain-matching only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:399
msgid "`store.putCookie(cookie, cb(err))`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:401
msgid ""
"Adds a new cookie to the store.  The implementation SHOULD replace any "
"existing cookie with the same `.domain`, `.path`, and `.key` properties "
"-- depending on the nature of the implementation, it's possible that "
"between the call to `fetchCookie` and `putCookie` that a duplicate "
"`putCookie` can occur."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:403
msgid ""
"The `cookie` object MUST NOT be modified; the caller will have already "
"updated the `.creation` and `.lastAccessed` properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:405
msgid "Pass an error if the cookie cannot be stored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:407
msgid "`store.updateCookie(oldCookie, newCookie, cb(err))`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:409
msgid ""
"Update an existing cookie.  The implementation MUST update the `.value` "
"for a cookie with the same `domain`, `.path` and `.key`.  The "
"implementation SHOULD check that the old value in the store is equivalent"
" to `oldCookie` - how the conflict is resolved is up to the store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:411
msgid ""
"The `.lastAccessed` property will always be different between the two "
"objects (to the precision possible via JavaScript's clock).  Both "
"`.creation` and `.creationIndex` are guaranteed to be the same.  Stores "
"MAY ignore or defer the `.lastAccessed` change at the cost of affecting "
"how cookies are selected for automatic deletion (e.g., least-recently-"
"used, which is up to the store to implement)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:413
msgid ""
"Stores may wish to optimize changing the `.value` of the cookie in the "
"store versus storing a new cookie.  If the implementation doesn't define "
"this method a stub that calls `putCookie(newCookie,cb)` will be added to "
"the store object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:415
msgid "The `newCookie` and `oldCookie` objects MUST NOT be modified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:417
msgid "Pass an error if the newCookie cannot be stored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:419
msgid "`store.removeCookie(domain, path, key, cb(err))`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:421
msgid ""
"Remove a cookie from the store (see notes on `findCookie` about the "
"uniqueness constraint)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:423
msgid ""
"The implementation MUST NOT pass an error if the cookie doesn't exist; "
"only pass an error due to the failure to remove an existing cookie."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:425
msgid "`store.removeCookies(domain, path, cb(err))`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:427
msgid ""
"Removes matching cookies from the store.  The `path` parameter is "
"optional, and if missing means all paths in a domain should be removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:429
msgid "Pass an error ONLY if removing any existing cookies failed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:431
msgid "`store.removeAllCookies(cb(err))`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:433
msgid "_Optional_. Removes all cookies from the store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:435
msgid "Pass an error if one or more cookies can't be removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:437
msgid ""
"**Note**: New method as of `tough-cookie` version 2.5, so not all Stores "
"will implement this, plus some stores may choose not to implement this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:439
msgid "`store.getAllCookies(cb(err, cookies))`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:441
msgid ""
"_Optional_. Produces an `Array` of all cookies during `jar.serialize()`. "
"The items in the array can be true `Cookie` objects or generic `Object`s "
"with the [Serialization Format] data structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:443
msgid ""
"Cookies SHOULD be returned in creation order to preserve sorting via "
"`compareCookies()`. For reference, `MemoryCookieStore` will sort by "
"`.creationIndex` since it uses true `Cookie` objects internally. If you "
"don't return the cookies in creation order, they'll still be sorted by "
"creation time, but this only has a precision of 1ms.  See "
"`compareCookies` for more detail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:445
msgid "Pass an error if retrieval fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:447
msgid ""
"**Note**: not all Stores can implement this due to technical limitations,"
" so it is optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:449
msgid "MemoryCookieStore"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:451
msgid "Inherits from `Store`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:453
msgid ""
"A just-in-memory CookieJar synchronous store implementation, used by "
"default. Despite being a synchronous implementation, it's usable with "
"both the synchronous and asynchronous forms of the `CookieJar` API. "
"Supports serialization, `getAllCookies`, and `removeAllCookies`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:455
msgid "Community Cookie Stores"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:457
msgid ""
"These are some Store implementations authored and maintained by the "
"community. They aren't official and we don't vouch for them but you may "
"be interested to have a look:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:459
msgid ""
"[`db-cookie-store`](https://github.com/JSBizon/db-cookie-store): SQL "
"including SQLite-based databases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:460
msgid ""
"[`file-cookie-store`](https://github.com/JSBizon/file-cookie-store): "
"Netscape cookie file format on disk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:461
msgid ""
"[`redis-cookie-store`](https://github.com/benkroeger/redis-cookie-store):"
" Redis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:462
msgid ""
"[`tough-cookie-filestore`](https://github.com/mitsuru/tough-cookie-"
"filestore): JSON on disk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tough-cookie_README.md:463
msgid ""
"[`tough-cookie-web-storage-store`](https://github.com/exponentjs/tough-"
"cookie-web-storage-store): DOM localStorage and sessionStorage"
msgstr ""

